==>Features and Architecture of GIT :
   ---------------------------------
==>What is GIT ?:
  ---------------
-Git is a Distributed Version Control System Tool.
-Git is not acronym and hence no expansion.But most of the people abbreviated as Global Information Tracker.
-Git is developed by Linus Torvalds , who also developed Linux Kernal.
-Most of the companies like microsoft , facebook , Yahoo ,Linkedin ,Intel using the GIT as VCS tool.

==>Features of Git:
  -----------------
-->Git is very Popular because of the following reasons :
1)Distributed :
-------------
-Git is developed based on Distributed VCS Architecture.
     Because of Distributed architecture it has several advantages.
       a) Every developer has his own local repository and hence operations can be performed locally , thereby local repository and remote repository need not be connected always.
       
       b)all operations will be performed locally , hence performance if high when compared to other VCS.i.e it is very speed.
       
       c)most of the operations are local.Hence we can work offline most of the time.
       
       d)there is no single point of failure as every developer has his own local repository.
       
       e) it enables parallel development and automatic - backups.
2)Staging Area:
----------------
-It is also known as Index Area.
-There is a logical/virtula layer in git between working directory and local repository.
-we can not commit the files of working directory directly. first we have to add to the staging area and then we have to commit.
-Staging Area is helpful to double check/cross check our changes before commit.
-this type of layer is not available in other VCS tools like CVS , SVN etc.
-Git stores files in repository in some Hash form , which saves the space.
-Git internally uses Snapshot mechanism for this , all these conversions and taking snapshots of our data will be happened in staging Area before commit.

Eg:
-If a sample repository around 12GB space in SVN where as Git hardly 420MB.
-Hence Staging Area is most important strength of Git.

3)Branching and Merging :
------------------------
-we can create and work on multiple branches simultaneously and all these branches are isolated from each other.it enables multiple work flows.
- we can merge multiple branches into a single branch , we can commit branch wise also.
- Moving files in Git is very easy as GIT automatically tracks the moves.

-Freeware and Opensource.
-it provides support for multiple platforms.
